Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q13 (opened here: a 001 core test flaked once under make verify)
Why this approach: Submit sends under a read lock after checking closed, with a select default, so it never waits and never reaches a closed channel; Close sets closed under the write lock before closing the queue. Close waits for the workers one by one until its context is done, then cancels the workers' context (the in-flight SaveExchange gets it), waits for them to return, and releases and counts what is left. A worker that takes an item after the cancel releases it, counts it undrained and stops. The worker loop only calls SaveExchange and Release; T14 adds the rest. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T13").
Alternatives rejected: a blocking send with a timeout (a request would wait on capture); counting a Submit after Close apart from dropped_queue_full (the access line calls both dropped_queue_full, so the count follows the line); a separate goroutine to wait for all workers in Close (a sequential wait with a select on ctx needs no extra goroutine).
Trade-off / known limit: Close waits for every worker after the cancel, so a store that ignores its context would hold shutdown up. Counts has only DroppedQueueFull until T14. The sink tests build real exchanges through the core proxy with a sink that holds them, since an Exchange's reservation can't be made outside core; that is how they prove refused and undrained exchanges give their memory back.
Verified by: make verify; go test -race -count=3 ./internal/capture (TestCapture_StreamNotDelayed, TestCapture_QueueFullDrops, TestSink_SubmitAfterCloseReturnsFalse after_close / racing_close, TestSink_CloseCountsUndrained drained_in_time / deadline_passes), each with the leak check. Mutations, each reverted: a blocking send hung TestCapture_QueueFullDrops; no closed check panicked with send on closed channel; no Release on refusal failed both SubmitAfterClose subtests on InUse; no cancel hung deadline_passes; no ctx check in the worker made Close return 0. Leaving the sink open failed the leak check on a stack through capture.(*Sink).work. core's and anthropic's leak checks now also match internal/capture.
